rawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Defender"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Wall of Wood","oracle_id":"aa5e6894-8c97-46f8-a0fd-07c6db51e9a7","oracle_text":"Defender (This creature can't attack.)","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2007-07-13","toughness":"3","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Wall"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn't provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"06e0459f-d691-4470-884a-27c09b6612d2","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature type of a Sliver changes so it's no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures.","oracle_id":"06e0459f-d691-4470-884a-27c09b6612d2","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because damage remains marked on a creature until the damage is removed as the turn ends, nonlethal damage dealt to a Sliver may become lethal if Muscle Sliver leaves the battlefield during that turn.","oracle_id":"06e0459f-d691-4470-884a-27c09b6612d2","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Muscle Sliver's ability does give itself +1/+1.","oracle_id":"06e0459f-d691-4470-884a-27c09b6612d2","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn't provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"2c09ca09-8e62-4fe3-9b3d-61573dd2ffbc","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature type of a Sliver changes so it's no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures.","oracle_id":"2c09ca09-8e62-4fe3-9b3d-61573dd2ffbc","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Elvish Archdruid's first ability affects only other Elves you control. However, Elvish Archdruid's second ability counts all Elves you control \u2014 including itself.","oracle_id":"6e2c2423-d854-4478-99e6-64f29851f026","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Elvish Archdruid's activated ability is a mana ability. It doesn't use the stack and players can't respond to it.","oracle_id":"6e2c2423-d854-4478-99e6-64f29851f026","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Hivestone doesn't affect creature spells or creature cards anywhere other than the battlefield.","oracle_id":"72aeed80-653b-4c53-ba65-a339aad14b9a","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Slivers are unaffected by Hivestone; a creature can't have the same creature type twice.","oracle_id":"72aeed80-653b-4c53-ba65-a339aad14b9a","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn\u2019t provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"7d592d5b-95cf-4416-9ade-1c23a8ba01d1","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it\u2019s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.","oracle_id":"7d592d5b-95cf-4416-9ade-1c23a8ba01d1","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It affects Elves controlled by all players, not just yours.","oracle_id":"7e40f37c-9a0c-40e0-b195-7ea94b12f798","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card is now an Elf but has been reworded so that it does not give itself the bonus.","oracle_id":"7e40f37c-9a0c-40e0-b195-7ea94b12f798","published_at":"2005-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Kindred is a card type that allows noncreature cards to have creature types. For example, Echoes of Eternity is an Eldrazi (although not a creature) while on the battlefield and an Eldrazi card (although not a creature card) in zones other than the battlefield.","oracle_id":"997d2f38-5a50-451e-bd48-e36dcb24d967","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This cards was originally printed with the \"tribal\" card type. That card type has been replaced with \"kindred\". This change does not affect the gameplay function of this card.","oracle_id":"997d2f38-5a50-451e-bd48-e36dcb24d967","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While it appears only on cards that already have other card types, kindred is a card type and will be counted by effects that refer to the number of card types among cards in a zone.","oracle_id":"997d2f38-5a50-451e-bd48-e36dcb24d967","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Graaz loses its abilities for some reason, then Juggernauts you control will not have to attack each combat and will be able to be blocked by Walls. However, due to how continuous effects are applied in layers, other creatures you control will continue to be 5/3 Juggernauts in addition to their other types. Unstoppable, indeed!","oracle_id":"aebfdcc0-c5b9-4737-8498-764a5021b087","published_at":"2023-02-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type (such as by Sea's Claim), it continues to be a creature and a Dryad.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although originally printed with a characteristic-defining ability that defined its color, this card now has a color indicator. This color indicator can't be affected by text-changing effects (such as the one created by Crystal Spray), although color-changing effects can still overwrite it.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dryad Arbor is played as a land. It doesn't use the stack, it's not a spell, it can't be responded to, it has no mana cost, and it counts as your land play for the turn.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Due to its color indicator (appearing to the left of its type line), Dryad Arbor is green. Color indicators apply in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Forest is a land type and Dryad is a creature type.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dryad Arbor is changed into another basic land type, it continues to be a green Dryad creature.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a Dryad Arbor gains flash, or you have the ability to play Dryad Arbor as though it had flash (due to Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir or Scout's Warning, for example), you can ignore the normal timing rules for when during your turn you can play a land, but not any other restrictions. You can't play Dryad Arbor during another player's turn, and you can't play Dryad Arbor if you don't have any land plays remaining.","oracle_id":"e996cd67-739c-40f4-b276-0042acf26c71","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"With a Humility and two Opalescences on the battlefield, if Humility has the latest timestamp, then all creatures are 1/1 with no abilities. If the timestamp order is Opalescence, Humility, Opalescence, the second Opalescence is 1/1, and the Humility and first Opalescence are 4/4. If Humility has the earliest timestamp, then everything is 4/4.","oracle_id":"ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0","published_at":"2006-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Removes all creature abilities. This includes mana abilities. Animated lands will also lose the ability to tap for mana.","oracle_id":"ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is the current interaction between Humility and Opalescence:\u00a0The type-changing effect applies at layer 4, but the rest happens in the applicable layers. The rest of it will apply even if the permanent loses its ability before it's finished applying. So if Opalescence, Humility, and Worship are on the battlefield and Opalescence entered before Humility, the following is true: Layer 4: Humility and Worship each become creatures that are still enchantments. (Opalescence). Layer 6: Humility and Worship each lose their abilities. (Humility) Layer 7b: Humility becomes 4/4 and Worship becomes 4/4. (Opalescence). Humility becomes 1/1 and Worship becomes 1/1 (Humility). But if Humility entered before Opalescence, the following is true: Layer 4: Humility and Worship each become creatures that are still enchantments (Opalescence). Layer 6: Humility and Worship each lose their abilities (Humility). Layer 7b: Humility becomes 1/1 and Worship becomes 1/1 (Humility). Humility becomes 4/4 and Worship becomes 4/4 (Opalescence).","oracle_id":"ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Under Dralnu's Crusade, Goblins are black only, not black in addition to any other colors. They are, however, Zombies in addition to their other creature types. As one enters the battlefield, it is already a black Goblin Zombie (and perhaps some other creature types) with +1/+1; it doesn't enter and then become a black Goblin Zombie and get +1/+1.","oracle_id":"ff48cf80-4950-4ae4-9f7c-8d826b2f26f7","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
